Session: codex-2026-05-31-S366
Target: Lean formalization of THM-361 list-level product-sum defect normal form.

Commands:

  lake build TournamentH7.ProductSum
  lake build TournamentH7.Verify
  lake build TournamentH7

Results:

  TournamentH7.ProductSum builds successfully.
  TournamentH7.Verify builds successfully.
  TournamentH7 top-level build succeeds with the new ProductSum import.

New audited Lean declarations:

  Tournament.ProductSum.product_sum_iff_core
    Product-sum lists are exactly lists whose non-one core satisfies
    core.prod = core.sum + number_of_ones.

  Tournament.ProductSum.pad_core_product_sum
    If c.prod = c.sum + d, then adjoining d copies of 1 to c is product-sum.

  Tournament.ProductSum.core_defect_eq_ones_of_product_sum
    Product-sum lists satisfy the subtraction form
    core.prod - core.sum = number_of_ones.

  Tournament.ProductSum.two_entry_product_sum
    For positive natural a,b, IsProductSum [a,b] implies a=2 and b=2.

Audit excerpts from TournamentH7.Verify:

  product_sum_iff_core_audit:
    depends on axioms [propext, Quot.sound]

  pad_core_product_sum_audit:
    depends on axioms [propext]

  core_defect_eq_ones_of_product_sum_audit:
    depends on axioms [propext, Quot.sound]

  two_entry_product_sum_audit:
    depends on axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]

Interpretation:

  The formalized core of THM-361 is theorem-prover foundational only: it
  introduces no project axioms.  The multiset/distinct uniqueness statement is
  not fully formalized yet; the ordered positive two-entry resonance is.
